title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547387-the-world-of-despoina-shard?p=1547457#post1547457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> might very well be! I am not going to get too much into details about the gods and their true nature, at least no for now. Who knows? Maybe I'll give epic campaigns a look further down the road.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> Can't say anything about previous projects, maybe I will, maybe I won't, hard for me to say for sure. As for the updating order- by book and by alphabet, as I generally update stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, the Ascending Ones are now up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! Looking particularly forward to what the MM, Lucifuge, and whatever the hell will come from the Cainites","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T08:31:27-08:00","id":1547516,"title":"","content":"Cheiron is up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-10T14:18:28-08:00","id":1547672,"title":"","content":"Really enjoying reading through the Despoina stuff! I always occasionally find myself checking back to your Chronicles of Lost Light blog and Encyclopedia of Darkness doc too!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-11T13:46:50-08:00","id":1547686,"title":"","content":"So, important note on and project.<br /> <br /> Basically, I got stuck. Every time I wrote a new nation I just felt... bored? While it was a nice exercise, it felt like all I do is take the existing material and giving it some face paint. Now, there's nothing bad about it, but it just didn't hit the vibe I wanted- making something weird and eldritch that feels <i>new</i>. So after giving it a lot of thought, I made a decision to revise everything I've written. It wasn't an easy decision, especially as I know that people have already started reading the project, but it just felt like it is going nowhere and that I needed a new attitude. <br /> <br /> This new attitude was doing the opposite of what I originally planned- as I mentioned, the plan was to focus around the nations and using the gods as some plot device in the background. However, I decided to go on the complete opposite direction- each conspiracy's entry is going to be described through a god, with the society around the god being described as the cult which worships it without understanding exactly what it is. Currently, the AKD have their own god presented, the Labyrinth, and I say that I am far more satisfied with the result compared to the original presentation. I might add actual nations later down the line (after solving the conspiracies), but they are not going to merely reflect the conspiracies, even if they are influenced by them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hope you will like the project's new direction even if you liked the original material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-11T14:37:27-08:00","id":1547687,"title":"","content":"Maybe you should have an in universe reason for a large area of your world to have a cosmopolitan culture. Example: An Empire that was supported by a pantheon of gods fell a couple of hundred years earlier. The old ekcumenical language is still mainly understood everywhere the old Empire ruled and was backed by the god of language and writing. However, now that the central Imperial authority is gone, linguistic driff is beginning to make communication harder.<br /> <br /> The differences between the old culture and the local societies would be what you'd need to cover.<br /> <br /> More distinctive societies on the edges of the old Empire would require more details but since the lands of the old empire were covered more compactly you'd have the room in page count to cover them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T05:56:47-08:00","id":1547846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547387-the-world-of-despoina-shard?p=1547687#post1547687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you should have an in universe reason for a large area of your world to have a cosmopolitan culture. Example: An Empire that was supported by a pantheon of gods fell a couple of hundred years earlier. The old ekcumenical language is still mainly understood everywhere the old Empire ruled and was backed by the god of language and writing. However, now that the central Imperial authority is gone, linguistic driff is beginning to make communication harder.<br /> <br /> The differences between the old culture and the local societies would be what you'd need to cover.<br /> <br /> More distinctive societies on the edges of the old Empire would require more details but since the lands of the old empire were covered more compactly you'd have the room in page count to cover them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's always an empire, isn't there?<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I am currently focused around using the gods as pieces of worldbuilding, it would take a while before I engage with countries properly, though I do try to express aspects of the cultures of Despoina through the cult sections in each god's entry. And on this note, I have just finished the Core Eight conspiracies. Fun fact- even if you are to use a regular setting, it is likely that those &quot;gods&quot; could be integrated as part of the setting for the &quot;true source of the Endowments&quot;, if you would be interested in exploring that angle!<br /> <br /> Anyway, next move- the supplementary conspiracies, starting for the specialized ones!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T14:35:59-08:00","id":1547863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547387-the-world-of-despoina-shard?p=1547846#post1547846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there's always an empire, isn't there?<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I am currently focused around using the gods as pieces of worldbuilding, it would take a while before I engage with countries properly, though I do try to express aspects of the cultures of Despoina through the cult sections in each god's entry. And on this note, I have just finished the Core Eight conspiracies. Fun fact- even if you are to use a regular setting, it is likely that those &quot;gods&quot; could be integrated as part of the setting for the &quot;true source of the Endowments&quot;, if you would be interested in exploring that angle!<br /> <br /> Anyway, next move- the supplementary conspiracies, starting for the specialized ones!</div> </div> </div> </div>I especially curious on how you will handle the cainites considering their nature. Would have for les mysteres but I assume youre going with a more organized &quot;theology&quot; (as they would have it) as it fits your setting more<br /> <br /> I am a bit confused with the Madonna and the Faith. The Malleus Maleficarum equivalent here is decidedly only monotheistic when enforced, and that's what they plan to do. It makes sense, as having a more traditional monotheistic &quot;God&quot; would easily make it seem like the other gods are lesser. A good choice in my opinion. However I can't help but feel they have a more Long Night feel to their god than a Malleus maleficarum one? Perhaps I'm looking at it wrong, and in this setting youre really hammering more into the aspect of them as an inquisition? Makes a lot of sense if thats the angle. At least it gets rid of the Long Night feel to their faith to me. Also, is this Ascending organization basing their faith on what's found in their country? I'd just like to know if this new prevailing ethos is founded upon what it's practitioners find in the country/similarities in other faiths or if it's just a power play based on a better understanding of what Faith is. It also kinda reminds me more of your take on les mysteres way back in your conspiracy theory/vigil ascendant thread<br /> <br /> as for the madonna, it kinda goes with the Faith. The Faith gets rid of a heaven/hell higher good and lower evil dichotomy, but the Madonna brings it right back in a seemingly objective existence (at least in her mind). What's the reasoning behind this choice? Especially since the two gods and cults don't seem to be connected in any way (admittedly, I'm more surprised by that since you love their relationship in Vigil)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 01-20-2025, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T05:01:49-08:00","id":1547873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547387-the-world-of-despoina-shard?p=1547863#post1547863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a bit confused with the Madonna and the Faith. The Malleus Maleficarum equivalent here is decidedly only monotheistic when enforced, and that's what they plan to do. It makes sense, as having a more traditional monotheistic &quot;God&quot; would easily make it seem like the other gods are lesser. A good choice in my opinion. However I can't help but feel they have a more Long Night feel to their god than a Malleus maleficarum one? Perhaps I'm looking at it wrong, and in this setting youre really hammering more into the aspect of them as an inquisition? Makes a lot of sense if thats the angle. At least it gets rid of the Long Night feel to their faith to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I follow? It sounds your question is about the cult rather than the god, and, well, the cult of Faith will behave differently from the MM because the circumstances are different. Like how the cult of the World Tree is different from the TFV. Is the &quot;Long Night&quot; feel is that there are numerous interpretations for the Faith rather than a single god? Because if that's so, as it was described, the Faith can only coherently manifest when there are enough people who believe in the same dogma, hence, as you mentioned, the Inquisition. The gods are not meant to translate one to one to what the conspiracies believe in. Rather, they are sources of power- and the cults more often than not interoperate them in a different manner. Faith, for example, is a transcendent truth that grants substance to any religion, but its faithful do not recognize this aspect, as they don't worship Faith knowingly. They worship whatever religion the believe in, and it is simply that Darwinistically, the more zealot and oppressive religions are the ones who gain the most members, and as such allow greater access to Faith. Syncretic religions don't work too well for Faith as it needs cohesive dogma to manifest, hence the cult it made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, is this Ascending organization basing their faith on what's found in their country? I'd just like to know if this new prevailing ethos is founded upon what it's practitioners find in the country/similarities in other faiths or if it's just a power play based on a better understanding of what Faith is. It also kinda reminds me more of your take on les mysteres way back in your conspiracy theory/vigil ascendant thread </div> </div> </div>The gods are mostly local entities. The cults of the gods are basically the blind men trying to describe the elephant through touch. All cults are the same in this regard. Some scholars might try to understand what is the truth behind &quot;divinity&quot;, having their own theological theories, some of which are accepted, others being branded as heresy. Most people just worship what the Imperial Cult tells them to worship. Faith is meant to be weirder god than the rest as unlike the other gods, it can only be worshipped when no gods is directly worshiped (hence when people &quot;worship their Faith alone&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as for the madonna, it kinda goes with the Faith. The Faith gets rid of a heaven/hell higher good and lower evil dichotomy, but the Madonna brings it right back in a seemingly objective existence (at least in her mind). What's the reasoning behind this choice? Especially since the two gods and cults don't seem to be connected in any way (admittedly, I'm more surprised by that since you love their relationship in Vigil) </div> </div> </div>I don't think that Faith removes Hell in any way? Like, it is a fantasy setting, obviously there will be some kind of Hell. Faith is about religion and dogma- <i>why</i> you go to Hell and <i>subjective</i> perceptions of right and wrong is how Faith comes into the world. However, the Lucifuge can't exist without Hell because, well, that's their whole schtick. There is an infernal realm which is defined by Vice (not Evil explicitly). As such, there are demons, and the Madonna is a rogue archdemon who seeks redemption. The fact that there are subjective perceptions of good and evil while there is an objective realm of torture and vice do not contradict one another. It makes things <i>weird</i>, sure, but it is a weird world. This is also why the Madonna and Faith do not explicitly interact with each other (as most gods do not interact)- each god kinda do its own thing, with its own cosmological truth and its own place in reality. This is why the world sucks- even the least hostile gods (the Gods of the Candle) do not work with each other or coordinate with each other, which creates the divine entropy that brings monsters to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T15:00:06-08:00","id":1547899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547387-the-world-of-despoina-shard?p=1547873#post1547873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I follow? It sounds your question is about the cult rather than the god, and, well, the cult of Faith will behave differently from the MM because the circumstances are different. Like how the cult of the World Tree is different from the TFV. Is the &quot;Long Night&quot; feel is that there are numerous interpretations for the Faith rather than a single god? Because if that's so, as it was described, the Faith can only coherently manifest when there are enough people who believe in the same dogma, hence, as you mentioned, the Inquisition. The gods are not meant to translate one to one to what the conspiracies believe in. Rather, they are sources of power- and the cults more often than not interoperate them in a different manner. Faith, for example, is a transcendent truth that grants substance to any religion, but its faithful do not recognize this aspect, as they don't worship Faith knowingly. They worship whatever religion the believe in, and it is simply that Darwinistically, the more zealot and oppressive religions are the ones who gain the most members, and as such allow greater access to Faith. Syncretic religions don't work too well for Faith as it needs cohesive dogma to manifest, hence the cult it made.<br /> <br /> <br /> The gods are mostly local entities. The cults of the gods are basically the blind men trying to describe the elephant through touch. All cults are the same in this regard. Some scholars might try to understand what is the truth behind &quot;divinity&quot;, having their own theological theories, some of which are accepted, others being branded as heresy. Most people just worship what the Imperial Cult tells them to worship. Faith is meant to be weirder god than the rest as unlike the other gods, it can only be worshipped when no gods is directly worshiped (hence when people &quot;worship their Faith alone&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think that Faith removes Hell in any way? Like, it is a fantasy setting, obviously there will be some kind of Hell. Faith is about religion and dogma- <i>why</i> you go to Hell and <i>subjective</i> perceptions of right and wrong is how Faith comes into the world. However, the Lucifuge can't exist without Hell because, well, that's their whole schtick. There is an infernal realm which is defined by Vice (not Evil explicitly). As such, there are demons, and the Madonna is a rogue archdemon who seeks redemption. The fact that there are subjective perceptions of good and evil while there is an objective realm of torture and vice do not contradict one another. It makes things <i>weird</i>, sure, but it is a weird world. This is also why the Madonna and Faith do not explicitly interact with each other (as most gods do not interact)- each god kinda do its own thing, with its own cosmological truth and its own place in reality. This is why the world sucks- even the least hostile gods (the Gods of the Candle) do not work with each other or coordinate with each other, which creates the divine entropy that brings monsters to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i understand they're not gonna be a 1 to 1, let me rephrase<br /> <br /> I thought the reason you made their god have to due with Faith and faith (in a way) alone was due to not having a concept of heaven or hell in the traditional sense to the setting. So I was surprised when the Madonna was quite explicitly from a &quot;heaven&quot; so to speak and fell to &quot;hell&quot;. Like there is a hell associated with Vice, but seemingly not a heaven linked to Virtue. <br /> <br /> In short, I'm surprised there seems to be an objective demon figure, but not an angelic one (splitting hairs that the Madonna used to be)<br /> <br /> Its more likely I'm just surprised the two gods weret more linked. I do like your new take on the setting as it feels a LOT more like a different yet faithful take rather than a scaled up one, don't get me wrong. I just remember you yourself liking the links between lucifuge and Baudolino and thought you would carry that aspect over to the setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T05:38:35-08:00","id":1547907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547387-the-world-of-despoina-shard?p=1547899#post1547899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh i understand they're not gonna be a 1 to 1, let me rephrase<br /> <br /> I thought the reason you made their god have to due with Faith and faith (in a way) alone was due to not having a concept of heaven or hell in the traditional sense to the setting. So I was surprised when the Madonna was quite explicitly from a &quot;heaven&quot; so to speak and fell to &quot;hell&quot;. Like there is a hell associated with Vice, but seemingly not a heaven linked to Virtue.<br /> <br /> In short, I'm surprised there seems to be an objective demon figure, but not an angelic one (splitting hairs that the Madonna used to be)<br /> <br /> Its more likely I'm just surprised the two gods weret more linked. I do like your new take on the setting as it feels a LOT more like a different yet faithful take rather than a scaled up one, don't get me wrong. I just remember you yourself liking the links between lucifuge and Baudolino and thought you would carry that aspect over to the setting</div> </div> </div> </div>In general I prefer that in this setting the gods will be separate from one another. Now, mortal cults might work together (there isn't a map, but I conceptualize the Libitanian Hills as being not that far away from the Saturnian Coast), but gods are just, well, gods. Each does their own shtick. <br /> <br /> As for the existence of an angel figure, well, <i>weaves towards the Knights of St Adrian</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T06:13:53-08:00","id":1547908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1547387-the-world-of-despoina-shard?p=1547907#post1547907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In general I prefer that in this setting the gods will be separate from one another. Now, mortal cults might work together (there isn't a map, but I conceptualize the Libitanian Hills as being not that far away from the Saturnian Coast), but gods are just, well, gods. Each does their own shtick.<br /> <br /> As for the existence of an angel figure, well, <i>weaves towards the Knights of St Adrian</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha! And I'm sorry if it seemed I was bashing the choices. I really like what you got so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T05:35:26-08:00","id":1548089,"title":"","content":"So, while my focus is currently on rebuilding Endowments (which from my POV is closely related to developing the gods), I don't want to leave this project &quot;hanging&quot;, so here is some summary about who the gods are for all canon conspiracies. I will add compacts, homebrew and a few exotic stuff in a different post.<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru- <b>Ariadna</b>, the Labyrinth, a living geomantic matrix that manifest itself through designed architecture and relic placement, dedicated to re-create the fallen paradise<br /> <br /> Ascending Ones- <b>Aten</b>, the Flame, a roaming pillar of smokeless fire which transmute the world around it from evil into good and from darkness into light<br /> <br /> Asclepeion- <b>Apollo</b>, the Sun, a solar entity born out of the sun itself which acts to burn out anything it deems to be &quot;impure&quot; by cleansing their taint<br /> <br /> Cainite Heresy- <b>Minerva</b>, the Warden, a divine fountain of blood which imbues those who spill their own blood into it with protection from the undead<br /> <br /> Campion Wildlife Services- <b>Artemis</b>, the Beast, a social construct which guides those imbued by it to take out those who create beasts through ritual hunting costumes<br /> <br /> Cheiron Group- <b>Chiron</b>, the Healer, a conglomeration of flesh which seeks to create a &quot;vaccine&quot; against monsters through experimentation and sharing its own flesh<br /> <br /> Council of Bones- <b>Anubis</b>, the Death, a rotting collective of numerous ghost shells that is drawn to sites of death and murder patterns<br /> <br /> Enigmatics- <b>Charis</b>, the Inspiration, a roaming spark of celestial light which ignites the imagination of those who view it with cursed imageries<br /> <br /> Faithful of Shulpae- <b>Ammut</b>, the Hunger, an empty cave within a hollow mountain which yearns to be fed with flesh, souls, and supernatural power<br /> <br /> Hototogisu- <b>Izanami</b>, the Thief, a strange musical entity which nets in the minds of those who listen to it and steals the bodies and powers of others<br /> <br /> Knights of St Adrian- <b>Metatron</b>, the Machine, a occult mechanism that brands those loyal to it with power to stop the entities born from its malfunctioning<br /> <br /> Knights of St George- <b>Baphomet</b>, the Sleep, a living nightmare which anchors itself to the minds of those loyal to it in order to inhibit magic<br /> <br /> Les Mysteres- <b>Epona</b>, the Rider, a spiritual principle which manifest itself through countless smaller spirits which communes with the living through an act of possession<br /> <br /> Lucifuge- <b>Lucifuge</b>, the Madonna, a demonic entity which exists as a living bloodline which seeks to redeem itself through its descendants<br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum- <b>Michael</b>, the Faith, a transcendent concept of divinity from which all forms of dogma and religion are derived<br /> <br /> Merrick Institute- <b>Mars</b>, the War, a primordial fear expressed through artistic representations that reaps the souls of children from their bodies<br /> <br /> Operation Nebula- <b>Itzpapalotl,</b> the Stranger, an alien thing which fell from the heavens in the form of dark fluid which thrives in the imagination of those who drink it<br /> <br /> Otodo- <b>Susanoo</b>, the Stormbringer, a manifestation of violence born from taint which birth children to manifest its endless wrath<br /> <br /> Survivor Club- <b>Tezcatlipoca</b>, the Enemy, a contagious shadow which resides in the hearts of murderers yet demands their death and propagate by infecting their survivors<br /> <br /> Task Force: VALKYRIE- <b>Odin</b>, the World Tree, a constructed intelligence built through mathematical algorithms that acts as a god of civilization<br /> <br /> VASCU- <b>Themis</b>, the Mirror, a dormant cognitive pattern which lives within the collective subconscious and enforce the concepts of &quot;humanity&quot; and &quot;justice&quot;<br /> <br /> Watchers- <b>Isis</b>, the Star, a distant light which communes through calendrical divination and megaliths to warn against coming calamities<br /> <br /> White Hare Society- <b>Hermes</b>, the Pathfinder, a spiritual pattern which lives through the veil between worlds and emanates through dimensional gateways","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}